{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-ccg-crossed-module-structure","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Lemma","doco:Section"],"label":"lem:ccg-crossed-module-structure","kind":"lemma","title":"Crossed-module structure on $(\\mathrm{SU}_{q_n}(2), \\mathcal{O}_M^{\\times})$","proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-ccg-crossed-module-structure"],"cites":["references/yekutieli2010"],"tags":["crossed-module","central-extension","peiffer-identity","gerbe-band"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.LiftingDescent.ccg_crossed_module_structure","text":"ccg-crossed-module-structure.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/ccg-crossed-module-structure.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"lem:ccg-crossed-module-structure\"></a><p><em>At each level <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code>, the pair <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathrm{SU}_{q_n}(2), \\mathcal{O}_M^{\\times})</code> is a crossed module <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"yekutieli2010\">[yekutieli2010]</span>, with boundary <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\partial(a) = a \\cdot \\mathbf{1}</code> and conjugation action <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g \\cdot a = g a g^{-1}</code>.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/ccg-crossed-module-structure.md","heading":"Lemma","number":"5.10.4"}
